<SitePage title="About — Mortal Shell 2 Wiki" heading="About this guide" description="Who maintains this independent Mortal Shell II guide, what our articles cover, and how to understand our editorial identity and limitations.">

<section><h2>Our purpose and independence</h2>
<p>{SITE.name} helps players understand the game's exploration, Shell and weapon choices, bosses, progression and PC setup. Our guides organise related questions so that a player can choose a useful next step, recognise uncertainty and avoid confusing a reported problem with a confirmed feature.</p>
<p><strong>Unofficial fan guide. Not affiliated with Cold Symmetry or Playstack.</strong> The site is not a developer support service, a licensed game database or an official store. Using the game's name identifies the subject of our writing; it does not indicate endorsement.</p></section>
<section><h2>Who publishes the articles</h2>
<p>Articles are published under the collective label <strong>{SITE.name} editorial team</strong>. This is the site's editorial identity, not a named game developer, a professional esports organisation or a claim that several independently identified reviewers tested each page. The site operator handles publication and can be contacted through our <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.</p>
<p>Automated writing assistance is used to help draft and organise material. That does not turn a draft into a verified result. We do not attach invented personal biographies, playtime totals, hardware configurations or test results to that work. The <a href="/editorial/">editorial policy</a> explains the evidence required for a first-hand test claim and how we handle corrections.</p></section>
<section><h2>What you can expect from a guide</h2>
<p>Store and developer material can establish release details, named modes or published requirements. Player discussions can reveal a question worth answering, but a forum report alone does not establish the cause of a bug or a universal solution. Recommendations about practice order or troubleshooting are editorial advice and should state the conditions under which they may help.</p>
<p>A page's “Last updated” date concerns that page's editorial changes. It does not certify that every sentence was retested on that date. Guide labels describe the kind of editorial content, not official endorsement or personal testing. A source screenshot is not a screenshot from our own play session.</p></section>
<section><h2>Game images and intellectual property</h2>
<p>Game screenshots and promotional art illustrate the environments, characters and systems discussed here. Their use on the site does not transfer ownership or establish a licence for visitors to reuse them. Rights in Mortal Shell, the game, characters, logos and associated imagery remain with the respective owners. Our site text and editorial organisation are separate from those game assets.</p>
<p>If an image is misidentified or you hold rights in material that should be removed, send the page URL and enough information to identify the material. We review requests through the same contact channel used for corrections; an attribution or fan-site disclaimer is not a substitute for reviewing a legitimate rights concern.</p></section>
<section><h2>Contact and site policies</h2>
<p>Send questions or corrections to <a href={`mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}`}>{SITE.contactEmail}</a>. Please include the article URL and a specific correction rather than account credentials or a full game save. Read the <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a> for how reading the site and contacting us can involve data, and the <a href="/terms/">terms of use</a> for reuse and third-party links.</p></section>
</SitePage>
